# WebGL conformance results flow from the target to the outer assertion harness

Firefox repository `git:314d8065c5ad68c7e5c5f92d`, revision `1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b`. Scope: DOM Canvas WebGL conformance tests and the shared Mochitest harness. Languages in the cited files: JavaScript, HTML. File roles are listed in the metadata. No production WebGL implementation is claimed.

js-test-pre caches its document pathname and window.parent.webglTestHarness. reportTestResultsToHarness increments local pass/fail counts and calls that cached object when present. In the inspected embedding that receiver is mochi-single.window.webglTestHarness. Its reportResults ignores pathname and calls outer parent.ok(success, message). testPassed and testFailed feed this function; testFailed also appends failure markup and flushes buffered logs.

## Change impact

A change to `reportResults` can change the success and message values sent to the outer assertion harness. A change to the cached parent receiver can affect every target using this version of `js-test-pre.js`. Membership in the wrapper family alone does not prove that an individual target imports this helper version.

**State:** RESULTS belongs to the target document; SimpleTest assertion state belongs to the outer wrapper. The exact parent.ok binding and assertion internals were not inspected.

**Special case:** reportSkippedTestResultsToHarness adds a fourth true argument, but this mochi-single receiver only uses success and message, so it does not propagate that skip marker separately.

## Evidence

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js` — `RESULTS; reportTestResultsToHarness; reportSkippedTestResultsToHarness`, lines 91–116](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js#L91-L116). Exact excerpt from lines 98–109:

```javascript
const locationPathname = window.location.pathname;
const webglTestHarness = window.parent.webglTestHarness;

function reportTestResultsToHarness(success, msg) {
  if (success) {
    RESULTS.pass += 1;
  } else {
    RESULTS.fail += 1;
  }
  if (webglTestHarness) {
    webglTestHarness.reportResults(locationPathname, success, msg);
  }
```

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js` — `testPassed; testFailed`, lines 221–246](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js#L221-L246). Exact excerpt from lines 238–246:

```javascript
function testFailed(msg) {
    msg = msg || 'Failed';
    if (_currentTestName)
      msg = _currentTestName + ': ' + msg;

    reportTestResultsToHarness(false, msg);
    _addSpan('<span><span class="fail">FAIL</span> ' + escapeHTML(msg) + '</span>');
    _bufferedLogToConsole('FAIL ' + msg);
    _flushBufferedLogsToConsole();
```

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochi-single.html` — `webglTestHarness.reportResults`, lines 19–26](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochi-single.html#L19-L26). Exact excerpt from lines 19–26:

```html
window.webglTestHarness = {
  reportResults(pathname, success, message) {
    if (parent) {
      parent.ok(success, message);
    } else {
      console.log('ok(' + success + ', \'' + message + '\')');
    }
  },
```

## Test links and validation

**Direct source-defined check, narrow scope:** The [always-fail sentinel](3a5b3b5d-3324-4080-9187-3196bf4a7aed.md) checks the deliberately failed assertion route. Other forwarding details, duplicate completion, async cleanup, and preference restoration are not directly asserted by this sentinel. **Execution-only:** The [inactive-attribute target](09ff632c-c5e0-445c-a5de-440fb21349eb.md) enters the shared harness. Other possible test links remain unverified.

The cited implementation, callers, and applicable receiver bodies were read. An independent source review accepted this scoped relationship with its listed gaps. No Firefox or Thunderbird product tests, generator run, or build ran for this evidence. There is no runtime pass/fail result. No Thunderbird–Firefox call chain is added by this Firefox-only slice.

